mode: "100644"
text: "# Brand Profile Template\n\nThis is the exact structure to write to `brand-profile.md`. Keep it **tight and skimmable** —\nother skills read it on every task, so favor specifics over prose. Delete sections that\ngenuinely don't apply (e.g., compliance for an unregulated business), but keep the order.\n\nCopy everything below the line into `brand-profile.md` and fill it in.\n\n---\n\n```markdown\n# Brand Profile — {Business or Client Name}\n<!-- version: 1.0 · last updated: {date} · review: quarterly or on rebrand/pivot/new offer\n     · type: {b2b-saas | ecommerce | local | services | personal | nonprofit | agency-client} -->\n\n## Identity\n- **What it is (one sentence):** {a stranger understands this}\n- **Category:** {the lane it competes in}\n- **Founded / location:** {if relevant — esp. local}\n\n## Positioning\n- **What's different:** {the one thing the alternatives don't do}\n- **Why believe it:** {the credible reason}\n- **Point of view:** {1–3 stances the brand will defend}\n- **Won't say:** {takes that are off-limits}\n\n## Audience\n### Segment 1 — {short label}\n- **Who:** {role/identity in plain terms}\n- **Cares about:** {goals / pains}\n- **Believes / objects:** {current mindset, friction}\n- **Where:** {platforms + mindset}\n- **Sophistication:** {beginner ↔ expert}\n### Segment 2 — {optional}\n- {same fields}\n- **Buyer vs follower note:** {if they differ}\n- **Transformation:** {before → after}\n\n## Voice\n- **Dimensions:** Formality {x/5} · Warmth {x/5} · Authority {x/5} · Energy {x/5} · Humor {x/5} · Polish {x/5}\n- **We sound ___, never ___:** {2–4 pairs — the most useful line in this file}\n- **Words we use:** {signature vocabulary, how we name product/customers/category}\n- **Words we ban:** {jargon, clichés, hype — be specific}\n- **How we handle hard things:** {price changes, mistakes, competitors}\n- **Signature devices:** {openers, rhythm, emoji policy, hashtag policy, punctuation, formatting}\n- **Voice by platform:** {only the shifts that matter}\n- **Pronunciation guide:** {brand/product/founder names voice tools must not mangle — phonetic}\n\n## Proof\n- **Numbers:** {customers, results, %}\n- **Named customers / logos (public-OK):** {list + any restrictions}\n- **Outcomes / case results:** {before → after results}\n- **Credentials / track record:** {years, awards, certifications}\n- **Social proof:** {reviews, ratings, community size}\n- **Usage rights note:** {which testimonials/UGC are cleared, and for what — organic reposting\n  and paid ads are DIFFERENT permissions; record which you hold}\n\n## Offers & CTAs\n- **Primary CTA:** {the main action}\n- **Secondary CTAs:** {follow, save, comment, join, read}\n- **Lead magnets / free tools / offers:** {what to point to}\n- **Hard-sell rules:** {e.g., \"never hard-sell on Reddit\"}\n\n## Channels\n- **Active platforms:** {the ones we actually post on}\n- **Posting cadence (if known):** {per platform}\n- **Handles / links:** {@ handles, site, link-in-bio}\n- **Languages / markets:** {content languages; market-specific voice or compliance shifts}\n\n## Operational defaults (tool skills read these)\n- **AI & synthetic media policy:** {disclosure stance — when/how we label AI-assisted content;\n  are AI avatars allowed? voice clones (own-voice-only, consent-verified)? AI music/imagery?\n  Any hard nos. Note: EU AI Act synthetic-media disclosure applies from Aug 2026 — set the\n  default now}\n- **Accessibility defaults:** {alt text on every image: yes/no+style; captions always-on for\n  video; contrast/plain-language notes}\n- **Visual identity:** → see design-and-templates / brand kit for logo, hex colors, and type\n  (don't duplicate here; one pointer keeps a single source of truth)\n\n## Guardrails\n- **Banned words/topics:** {hard nos}\n- **Compliance / legal:** {forbidden claims, required disclaimers, review needs — esp.\n  regulated industries}\n- **Competitor rules:** {name them? compare? never mention?}\n- **Sensitivity:** {topics to handle with care or avoid}\n\n## Show, don't tell — example posts\n- **Loves:** {3–5 posts (ours or others'), each with one line on *why*}\n- **Hates:** {1–2 posts + why}\n\n## Notes\n- {anything else a writer should know — seasonality, current campaign}\n```\n\n---\n\n## How other skills should read this\n\nTreat **Voice → \"We sound ___, never ___\"**, **Guardrails**, **Operational defaults**, and\n**Show-don't-tell examples** as the highest-signal sections — check them on every task.\nIdentity, Positioning, and Audience set the strategy; Proof and Offers/CTAs feed the\nspecifics and the close. Tool skills (avatars, voice, music, image generation) must check\n**Operational defaults** before generating anything synthetic. If a section is empty, ask\nthe user rather than inventing content to fill it.\n"
